17592186344356 #edb/ref 1080 "k=7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344356 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344356 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0d5b11f-4138-5c57-8bc8-f9f3a404cfaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343221 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186344356 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344664 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "6517af05-6089-578f-972a-9310f8010c94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186342477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343785 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186343955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186344129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186342477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344805 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b1cccc34-d274-5062-9c39-f9e811dad04c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344957 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344957 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74637" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344957 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344957 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 2x+3y=-1 \\\\  & x-2y=1 \\\\  & -x-5y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- The system has no solution\n- The system is consistent independent\n- The system is consistent dependent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344957 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b0089d19-a4b5-5ec4-beaa-917a294458ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344957 #edb/ref 1074 "To classify the system, we first try to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y=1 \\\\ 7y=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get $y=-\\frac{3}{7}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-\\frac{3}{7})=1\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\n \nSo, we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement II is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344961 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186344664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344961 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74646" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344961 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344961 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is inconsistent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+4y=2 \\\\  & 2x+(k+1)y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344961 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a0c28bd7-70de-59aa-93c9-933cbaca4593" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186344961 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k+1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & k-7 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+4y=2 \\\\ (k-7)y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is inconsistent if it has no solutions. For the system to have no solutions, one of the equations above must be false.\n\nIf $k=7,$ then the second equation is $0=-1,$ which is false, and the system will have no solution.\n\nTherefore, our system is inconsistent when $k=7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402009 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186402010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402009 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32247" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402009 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402009 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402009 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f65d67ed-b94b-50cc-87d4-9aa7130f7547" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402009 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 10 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -6 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe corresponding system is now  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+10{x}_{3}=-8 \\\\  & {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ and we have one free variable, ${x}_{3}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ in terms of ${x}_{3}.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2}=6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}={x}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{3}$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-8-10{x}_{3} \\\\ 6+6{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402012 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186402015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186402011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186402010 #edb/ref 