-b53a-8ca94675a39a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417077 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2+z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417077 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417077 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3937866-2599-550e-8d7d-230111af4c2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417078 #edb/ref 1080 "k=\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417078 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417078 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e23cbcca-7092-5855-aeeb-dd2de6061a27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417078 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417079 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "26b28742-5ee2-597a-8428-7062724625e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186417077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417077 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417080 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "40f01e87-54e2-5dd2-9850-20313302577b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417081 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417081 #edb/ref 1069 "q-32220" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417081 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417081 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+y+z=2 \\\\  & y+2z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417081 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "32425960-ceab-536a-8061-1f2469974e99" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417081 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the standard Gauss-Jordan method, we can reduce this matrix to reduced row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-z=2 \\\\  & y+2z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variables are $x$ and $y,$ and we have one free variable, $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ and $y$ in terms of $z.$ \n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+z \\\\ y=-2z \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $z$ (the free variable) is an arbitrary number.\n\nIn vector form, the latter can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2+z \\\\ -2z \\\\ z\\end{aligned}],\\,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417082 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417079 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417082 #edb/ref 1069 "q-131730" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417082 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417082 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine the value of $k$ for which the following system of linear equations is consistent dependent:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+2y=12 \\\\  & x+ky=4\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417082 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6deb5ca1-ae5b-5721-895d-6efa8ac5fdfb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186417082 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 1 & k & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2-3k & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+ky=4 \\\\  & (2-3k)y=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is consistent dependent if it has infinitely many solutions. For the system to have infinitely many solutions, it must have at least one free variable.\n\nIf $k=\\frac{2}{3},$ then the second equation is $0=0,$ which is true for any value of $y$, and we can remove this equation from the system. As a result, the system will contain only one equation, $x+ky=4.$ \n\nThen, the basic variable will be $x,$ and we will have a free variable $y.$ That means the system will have infinitely many solutions.\n\nTherefore, our system is consistent dependent when $k=\\frac{2}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
